cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper."
title: "puuwaawaa-normalization: score scaling in the Puʻuwaʻawaʻa spatial portfolio model"
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-07
abstract: >-
  Code for the normalization comparison (Appendix S1) and the Paddock 9
  structural sensitivity in the Puʻuwaʻawaʻa Forest Reserve structured
  decision making case study. It compares global linear, vector and
  within-unit scaling of the same criterion scores, and tests how fixing or
  freeing the Paddock 9 restoration commitment changes optimal portfolios
  under three specifications of conservation value and budgets from $0.5M
  to $60M.
